  "question": "Can a compact local classifier replace the existing Gemini blind forced-choice crop adjudicator on the frozen 1,131-instance probe with at least 95 percent pair coverage?",
  "answer": "Not under the declared contract. The model was exceptionally accurate where both literal forms existed in its 4,693-class training vocabulary (96.92 percent versus Gemini's 84.03 percent on 1,071 covered instances; paired delta +12.89 points, 95 percent CI +10.83 to +15.03), but pair coverage was 94.695 percent, 0.305 points below the frozen 95 percent hard gate. The missing side is usually a modern, erroneous, or corpus-absent alternative rather than a model failure, so this result rejects forced-choice replacement but motivates a separately frozen top-k evidence-channel evaluation.",
